  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(f(n)=\\dfrac{x_1+x_2+\\cdots+x_n}{n},\\) where \\(n\\) is a positive integer. If \\(x_k=(-1)^k,\\) \\(k=1,\\) \\(2,\\) \\(\\ldots,\\) \\(n,\\) the set of possible values of \\(f(n)\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\{0\\}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\left\\{\\dfrac1n\\right\\}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\left\\{0,-\\dfrac1n\\right\\}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\left\\{0,\\dfrac1n\\right\\}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\left\\{1,\\dfrac1n\\right\\}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(n\\) is even, the terms pair to give sum \\(0,\\) so \\(f(n)=0.\\) If \\(n\\) is odd, one final \\(-1\\) remains, so \\(f(n)=-\\frac{1}{n}.\\) The possible values are therefore \\(\\{0,-\\frac{1}{n}\\}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Pair consecutive terms \\(-1+1\\)",
        "Separate even and odd values of \\(n\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
